        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "কাছের (kāchher) is kāchh, \"nearness\", + -er, \"of\". CDIAL has no entry for kāchh, but it appears to belong with Sanskrit kakṣa, \"armpit, side\": there CDIAL lists Bengali kāṁkh, \"flank\", Nepali kāch, \"side, edge\", and Assamese kāxe, \"by the side of\", and notes that some words for \"beside\" probably grew from the sense \"side\" (CDIAL 2588)."
            }
          ]
        },
